{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":251971,"duration_api_ms":251010,"num_turns":38,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"810bb037-80e0-457c-99fe-aa9c27ddf504","total_cost_usd":1.73413625,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100133,"cache_read_input_tokens":1799670,"output_tokens":8334,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":100133,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":8334,"cacheReadInputTokens":1799670,"cacheCreationInputTokens":100133,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.73413625,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Thorough review of the concentration helper API implementation (tanksim-6e5.2.2). The core design is sound: a private `concentration()` function with NaN/Infinity/zero-volume guards, WaterState methods taking explicit `volume_l`, and TankState convenience methods that compute volume internally. All 17+ call sites migrated from `geometry.water_volume_l()` (gross volume) to `state.water_volume_l()` (net volume accounting for substrate displacement). Schema version bumped from 2→3 to prevent loading saves with stale volume semantics. Snapshot de-duplicated 6+ inline concentration calculations. Tests are comprehensive (8 tests including proptest for non-negativity). All tests pass, clippy is clean (only a pre-existing unrelated warning). The nitrogen cycle decomposer Monod kinetics and algae/plant half-saturation still use raw totals, but these are explicitly deferred to dependent tasks (6e5.2.3–2.5). Two minor issues found worth flagging.","amendments":[{"body":"In shrimp.rs, four private helper functions (shrimp_feeding, update_condition, update_molt_stress, emit_molt_stress_warning) still accept a `_volume_l: f64` parameter that is now dead code — each function either calls `state.water_volume_l()` or uses TankState concentration helpers internally. Remove the unused parameter from these private functions to avoid confusion and dead-code drift. The caller `step_daily_shrimp` already computes `volume_l` but it is only used as a zero-check guard; the helpers no longer need it passed in.","rationale":"Dead parameters in private functions create maintenance confusion: a future contributor may assume the parameter is being used or wonder whether the caller's volume and the helper's internally-computed volume could diverge. Since these are crate-private functions, removing the parameter is non-breaking and removes ~4 unused bindings."},{"body":"In nitrogen_cycle.rs line 83, the decomposer DO Monod term uses a hardcoded half-saturation constant (`do_total / (do_total + 2.0)`) with a comment '// half-sat ~2 mg total'. This constant should be extracted into ProcessParams (e.g., `decomposer_k_do_mg`) alongside the existing `decomposer_k_doc_mg`, so it is tunable and consistently documented. Currently it is the only hardcoded Monod K constant in the nitrogen cycle; all other guilds (AOB, NOB, comammox) have their K values in ProcessParams.","rationale":"Every other Monod half-saturation constant in the nitrogen cycle is in ProcessParams and therefore tunable and visible in data files. This lone hardcoded `2.0` is easy to miss during the upcoming kinetics normalization (tanksim-6e5.2.3) and creates an inconsistency in the parameter surface. Extracting it now avoids a latent bug where the normalization pass converts all K constants from total→concentration but misses this one because it's not in the params struct."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"95deab0c-0a65-4d85-89c8-69ce7c6aeda2"}
